{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggeSbUAVSnyd35EG44u7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dq and B cannot be determined for permanganate within the ligand-field model, so I am not giving values for them.\n\nMnO₄⁻ contains Mn(VII), which is d⁰. A Tanabe-Sugano analysis assumes d-d transitions between ligand-field terms, and a d⁰ configuration has no d electrons to excite. The three intense bands (17 570, 31 560 and 38 320 cm⁻¹, with ε of roughly 2 000–3 000 M⁻¹ cm⁻¹) are ligand-to-metal charge-transfer (O→Mn) bands. Their intensity is consistent with that assignment, since d-d bands are Laporte-forbidden and typically have ε of only a few tens to hundreds. Fitting these energies to Dq and B would be a category error, so any numbers produced would be meaningless. Because the ligand-field model does not apply to these bands, I did not run the fitting tools.\n\n{\"Dq\": null, \"B\": null, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": true, \"reason\": \"MnO4- is d0 and its bands are O-to-Mn charge-transfer transitions, not d-d ligand-field transitions, so Dq and B cannot be extracted.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8059,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8059,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dba471cb-6821-426c-ae3e-db1686720ca7","uuid":"82ec2756-c383-486d-aec1-7696303c99d4","timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:44:06.144Z","request_id":"req_011CggeSb67Dx6YcBpbM5eDA"}
